Event Normalization (Skill System)

1. Event Domains:

    Maximal Strength (MS)

        "How much force can the athlete produce in a single effort?"

        Failure occurs when required force exceeds the athlete’s maximum voluntary force output in a single effort.

        Any event which primarly focuses on maximal force output (primarly 1RM events).

    Strength Endurance (SE)

        "How long can the athlete produce submaximal force under fatigue?"

        Failure occurs when accumulated fatigue prevents continued force production at required submaximal intensity.

        Rep based events, medleys and events witha time cap.

    Athletic Power & Skill (APS)

        "How well can the athlete convert strength into speed, coordination, or 
        trajectory"

        Failure occurs when force cannot be applied quickly, accurately, or efficiently enough to meet the event’s movement demands.

        Events based around explosivity. Throws, dragging, and so on.

    Structural & Grip Resilience (SGR)

        "How well can the athlete tolerate sustained tension, awkward leverage, and pain?"

        Failure occurs when connective tissue, grip, or postural integrity can no longer tolerate sustained load.

        Events based arround "suffering". Grip holds, long/heavy carries long/heavy yoke walks.



2. Point Awarding Rules

    A. One Event one Domain

        A single event can only award points towards a single domain

    B. Event Disqualification / No Result

        Assign 0 pts

        Do NOT exclude from field size

    C. Event with ties

        Use shared placing

        Both athletes receive same percentile

    D. Skill Point bands and their Cases (8 athletes)

        Finals events use full percentile-based scoring (0–10).

        Group-stage events use compressed placement-based scoring (0–6).


    E. Percentile Calculation (formal definition)

        Percentile = 1 − ((Placing − 1) / (Field Size − 1))


    F. Finals events Skill Point Bands (0-10 pts)

        ≥ 95%	10 pts
        90–94%	9 pts
        80–89%	8 pts
        70–79%	7 pts
        60–69%	6 pts
        50–59%	5 pts
        40–49%	4 pts
        30–39%	3 pts
        20–29%	2 pts
        10–19%	1 pt
        < 10%	0 pts

    G. Group Stage Skill Point Bands (0–6 pts)

        ≥ 90%	6 pts
        80–89%	5 pts
        65–79%	4 pts
        50–64%	3 pts
        35–49%	2 pts
        20–34%	1 pt
        < 20%	0 pts


5. Domain Titles Awarding System

    A. Skill Points award one of 4 Titles.

        - Maximal Strength (MS) -> Static Monster 
        - Strength Endurance (SE) -> Hybrid Athlete 
        - Athletic Power & Skill (APS) -> Athletic Freak 
        - Structural & Grip Resilience (SGR) -> Technician
    
    B. A domain title gets awarded only after a givens domain skill points total is > 50

    C. Each athlete has four independent running totals:

        - MS_total
        - SE_total
        - APS_total
        - SGR_total

        After every event:
            Domain(new)​ = Domain(old) ​+ Event Skill Points
    


5. Lock-in Summary (rulebook)

One event → one domain

Percentile determines points

Fixed point bands

No split points